     I was playing a priest with the amulet on his way up through the dungeon
when the dungeon collapsed.  I had on a ring of conflict and ran across an Air
Elemental and a cockatrice.  The Air Elemental swallowed the cockatrice, turned
to stone and regurgitated the cockatrice.  Left on the screen was a statue of
an Air Elemental, an Air Elemental and no cockatrice.  The Air Elemental was
peaceful so I went searching for the cockatrice.  I took a couple of steps and
was attacked by a cockatrice but no one was in sight and I wasn,t blind.  I
took a couple of swings and finally a cockatrice appeared so I killed it.  I
then went back to the Air Elemental which was standing over the stairway going
up with no way to move it (no wand of teleportation or spell of teleport away). 
Remembering a post a few days ago about attacking peaceful monsters and
agravating your god, I threw a used up wand of striking at the Air Elemental. 
I then went over to it and began hitting it when I got the message:

relmon: mon not in list
The dungeon collapsed and the game said that I died of a panic.  I was playing
3.0.9 on a PC clone.  Lucky for me I copied the save file before I started to
play so that not too much playing time was wasted.  I am also sending this to
Nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu. Oh yea, almost forgot, no new files were
created so I assume that the game cannot be restored.

